$ python mapploid --help
usage: mapploid [-h] [--version] {prepare,call} ...

Infer plant ploidy: prepare reference regions, then analyze one or more BAM samples.

options:
  -h, --help      show this help message and exit
  --version       show the software version and exit

commands:
  {prepare,call}
    prepare       prepare reusable analysis regions from a reference FASTA
    call          infer ploidy for one BAM or a list of BAMs

Prepare the reference first:
  mapploid prepare --reference genome.fa --out reference_assets
Analyze one sample:
  mapploid call --bam sample.bam --assets reference_assets --out result
Analyze a batch:
  mapploid call --bam-list bams.txt --assets reference_assets --out batch_results

$ python mapploid prepare --help
usage: mapploid prepare [-h] --reference FASTA [--kmer BP]
                        [--min-region-length BP] --out DIR [--threads N]
                        [--exclude-bed BED] [--genmap-bedgraph FILE]

Prepare once per reference and region settings. Use the resulting --out
directory as call --assets.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --reference FASTA     reference genome as an uncompressed FASTA file
  --kmer BP             GenMap k-mer length in bp (default: 150)
  --min-region-length BP
                        minimum continuous high-mappability region length in
                        bp (default: 10000)
  --out DIR             directory to create, e.g. reference_assets; pass this
                        directory to call --assets
  --threads N           threads for reference preparation (default: 8)
  --exclude-bed BED     BED file of regions to exclude, e.g. organellar
                        sequences; may be repeated
  --genmap-bedgraph FILE
                        optional GenMap bedGraph made with the same reference,
                        k-mer length and 2 mismatches

$ python mapploid call --help
usage: mapploid call [-h] (--bam FILE | --bam-list FILE) --assets DIR --out
                     DIR [--sample NAME] [--keep-details] [--export-figures]
                     [--allele-min FLOAT] [--allele-max FLOAT] [--min-depth N]
                     [--max-depth N] [--min-mapq N] [--min-baseq N]
                     [--min-allele-reads N] [--pair-purity FLOAT]

Infer sample ploidy using the reference directory created by prepare.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --bam FILE            one sample BAM file, coordinate-sorted with a BAI/CSI
                        index
  --bam-list FILE       text file with one BAM path per line; each BAM must be
                        sorted and indexed
  --assets DIR          reference directory created by prepare --out, e.g.
                        reference_assets; shared by samples using the same
                        reference
  --out DIR             output directory: result.tsv for one sample, or a
                        summary and sample subdirectories for a batch
  --sample NAME         name for --bam only (default: BAM filename without
                        .bam); batches use each BAM filename
  --keep-details        retain stage tables and intermediate site data after
                        completion
  --export-figures      also export the report evidence figure as PDF and
                        300-dpi PNG

site filters (optional):
  --allele-min FLOAT    minimum frequency of each of the two leading alleles
                        (default: 0.15)
  --allele-max FLOAT    maximum frequency of each of the two leading alleles
                        (default: 0.85)
  --min-depth N         minimum site depth after quality filtering (default:
                        automatic)
  --max-depth N         maximum site depth after quality filtering (default:
                        automatic)
  --min-mapq N          minimum read mapping quality, 0-255 (default: 20)
  --min-baseq N         minimum base quality, 0-255 (default: 20)
  --min-allele-reads N  minimum supporting reads for each allele (default: 2)
  --pair-purity FLOAT   minimum fraction of valid base counts explained by the
                        two leading alleles (default: 0.95)

Examples:
  mapploid call --bam sample.bam --assets reference_assets --out result
  mapploid call --bam-list bams.txt --assets reference_assets --out batch_results

bams.txt: one BAM path per line; relative paths are resolved from the list directory.
Batch outputs: batch_results/result.tsv summarizes all samples;
               batch_results/samples/SAMPLE/ contains each sample's results and logs.

